<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>And to complete the information, the firmware is working using a copy of the original calibration (located at a specific location of the flash memory chip).<br>It never touch it (there is no even any code in the firmware to write at this specific location).<br><br>But it's always better to have a copy somewhere (eg: in case your flash chip dies, and you replace it).<br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel</div></blockquote>Hi Daniel, OFF topic question.<br><br>If a user accidentally flashes a wrong firmware, flashing openMDUV380.zip into a DM-1701 or openGD77.zip into a MDUV380, etc. Is there a possibility of messing up the original calibrations data?<br><br>Charlie,</div></blockquote>No, the firmware takes place in the MCU flash, not the external flash.<br><br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Tue Dec 31, 2024 3:57 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
