		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4723&amp;p=34970#p34970"><![CDATA[
And to complete the information, the firmware is working using a copy of the original calibration (located at a specific location of the flash memory chip).<br>It never touch it (there is no even any code in the firmware to write at this specific location).<br><br>But it's always better to have a copy somewhere (eg: in case your flash chip dies, and you replace it).<br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Tue Dec 31, 2024 2:37 pm</p><hr />
